+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Orders carry `discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, and a `coupon_code`, and the database
+already models coupons and coupon redemptions, but nothing lets a customer actually use a
+coupon. The endpoint `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` is requested so users can redeem
+fixed-amount and percentage coupons against a pending order.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": "SAVE20" }`.
+- Validate the request, the order, and the coupon (existence, active status, validity
+  window, minimum order amount, usage limit, and single-coupon-per-order).
+- Compute the discount for `FIXED` (cents) and `PERCENT` (0–100) coupons, apply the optional
+  `max_discount_cents` cap, and never discount below zero.
+- Persist the result on the order (`discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, `coupon_code`),
+  record a row in `coupon_redemptions`, and increment the coupon's `used_count` using the
+  injected `Clock`.
+- Return the updated order as JSON; failures return `{ error: { code, message } }` with an
+  UPPER_SNAKE code, consistent with the rest of the service.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `coupon-redemption`: Applying an active, eligible coupon to a pending order, including
+  discount calculation, order/persistency side effects, and rejection rules.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- None: no existing capability specs change. -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/routes/orders.ts`: register the new route.
+- `src/services/orderService.ts`: add the apply-coupon business logic.
+- `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts`: persist the applied coupon on the order.
+- `src/repositories/couponRepository.ts`: increment `used_count` and insert a redemption.
+- `src/app.ts`: wire any new dependencies.
+- No breaking API changes; `POST /orders`, `GET /orders`, pay, cancel, and coupon admin are
+  unchanged.
