+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository persistence
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(id, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents)` that updates the order's discount columns, verified by a focused unit check that the row reflects the new values.
+- [x] 1.2 Add `CouponRepository.redeem(orderId, code, discountCents, createdAt)` that increments `used_count` and inserts the `coupon_redemptions` row, verified by a focused check that both the counter and the redemption row change.
+
+## 2. Service rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Add `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` with request validation and order/coupon lookup (INVALID_REQUEST, ORDER_NOT_FOUND, COUPON_NOT_FOUND), verified by tests for each error path.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement eligibility checks (ORDER_NOT_PENDING, ORDER_ALREADY_HAS_COUPON, COUPON_DISABLED, COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID, COUPON_EXPIRED, COUPON_USAGE_LIMIT_REACHED, ORDER_BELOW_MIN_AMOUNT) using the injected Clock, verified by tests for each rejection.
+- [x] 2.3 Implement discount calculation for FIXED and PERCENT with `maxDiscountCents` cap and non-negative clamp, verified by tests for fixed, percent, cap, and over-amount cases.
+- [x] 2.4 Persist the applied coupon and redemption and return the updated order, verified by a test asserting the returned totals, `usedCount`, and redemption row.
+
+## 3. HTTP wiring
+
+- [x] 3.1 Wire the `CouponRepository` into `OrderService` in `src/app.ts` and register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`, verified by an end-to-end `app.request` test returning 200 with the discounted order.
+- [x] 3.2 Run `npm run build` and `npm test` and confirm both succeed with the new behavior.
+
+## 4. End-to-end verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Verify the endpoint against every scenario in `specs/coupon-redemption/spec.md` (success, each rejection, and side effects) with tests, and confirm existing order/coupon tests still pass.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after review requirements are satisfied.
